                <pb facs="0692" n="606" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg606"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Meyer to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1903-01-02"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 2,
                    1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Meyer reports that the Italian Government desire him to convey their
                    sentiments of gratitude to the President for his good offices, and to say that
                    Italy has no objection, as heretofore stated, to refer her claims to arbitration
                    at The Hague. The Italian Government are communicating with the cabinets at
                    London and Berlin concerning the other points at issue.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
